{"mechanism_label":"custom","params":{"Vmax":10.0,"Km":2.0,"Ki":1.0,"n":2.0},"custom_code":"PARAMS=['Vmax','Km','Ki','n']
def predict(df,p):
    S=df['S'].values; I=df['I'].values
    Kapp=p['Km']*(1.0+(I/p['Ki'])**p['n'])
    return p['Vmax']*S/(Kapp+S)","confidence":0.6,"reasoning":"The plateau near Vmax ≈ 10 at high S is preserved under all inhibitor levels while the apparent Km rises, which points to a competitive mechanism. The apparent Km factor (about 1, 1.15, 2, 5 at I = 0, 0.5, 1, 2) grows faster than linearly in I, which simple competitive inhibition cannot produce, so I used a cooperative competitive form, Km(1+(I/Ki)^n)."}
